g"}],"covers":[41347],"isbn_13":["9780060936389"],"isbn_10":["006093638X"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"On September 6, 1522, a battered ship appeared on the horizon near the port of Sanlucar de Barrameda, Spain."},"lc_classifications":["G420.M2B47 2003","G420.M2 B47 2004"],"source_records":["promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-07-15:T2-BAR-047","bwb:9780060936389","amazon:006093638X","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-04-22:P7-BMF-417","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-04-09:O6-ATQ-471","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:204720505:1554"],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:T2-BAR-047","urn:bwbsku:P7-BMF-417","urn:bwbsku:O6-ATQ-471","urn:nuls:31786101954482"],"key":"/books/OL7285308M","number_of_pages":512,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2655768W"}],"oclc_numbers":["57226539"],"latest_revision":17,"revision":17,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-03-08T00:30:55.187184"}},{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["867000"],"librarything":["68534"]},"title":"Over the Edge of the World","subtitle":"Magellan's Terrifying Circumnavigation of the Globe","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL387244A"}],"publish_date":"October 14, 2003","publishers":["William Morrow"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"covers":[52688],"isbn_13":["9780066211732"],"isbn_10":["0066211735"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"On June 7, 1494, Pope Alexander VI divided the world in half, bestowing the western portion on Spain, and the eastern on Portugal."},"source_records":["amazon:0066211735"],"key":"/books/OL7293340M","number_of_pages":480,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2655768W"}],"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-24T08:38:37.722035"}},{"publishers":["William Morrow"],"number_of_pages":458,"subtitle":"Magellan's terrifying circumnavigation of the globe","ia_box_id":["IA148315"],"isbn_10":["006093638","0066211735"],"pagination":"xvi, 458 p., [16] p. of plates :","covers":[7146790],"ia_loaded_id":["overedgeofworl00berg"],"key":"/books/OL23271376M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL387244A"}],"ocaid":"overedgeofworl00berg","publish_places":["New York"],"subjects":["Magalhães, Fernão de, -- d. 1521 -- Travel","Explorers -- Portugal -- Biography","Voyages around the world"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"genres":["Biography"],"source_records":["marc:CollingswoodLibraryMarcDump10-27-2008/Collingswood.out:59460890:2030","ia:overedgeofworl00berg","marc:marc_openlibraries_phillipsacademy/PANO_FOR_IA_05072019.mrc:35991536:1213","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run03.mrc:44841308:2440","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part30.utf8:190418077:1030","bwb:9780066211732","marc:marc_scms/20220805_ADAM_MARC_records.mrc:80106735:2783","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:225665257:2920","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:196303634:996","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_046.bib.mrc:112195671:5105"],"title":"Over the edge of the world","lccn":["2003050143"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. [431]-439) and index."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["867000"],"librarything":["68534"]},"edition_name":"1st ed.","local_id":["urn:phillips:31867001382857","urn:sfpl:31223049188270","urn:sfpl:31223050640797","urn:sfpl:31223062405361","urn:sfpl:31223049187728","urn:scms:0188600491149","urn:bwbsku:P7-DZF-379"],"publish_date":"2003","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Laurence Bergreen.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2655768W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["G420.M2 B47 2003","G420.M2B47 2003"],"oclc_numbers":["52047431"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Publisher's description: Ferdinand Magellan's daring circumnavigation of the globe in the sixteenth century was a three-year odyssey filled with sex, violence, and amazing adventure. Now in Over the Edge of the World, acclaimed author Laurence Bergreen, interweaving a variety of candid, first-person accounts, some previously unavailable in English, brings to life this groundbreaking and majestic tale of discovery that changed many long-held views about the world and the way explorers would henceforth navigate its oceans. In 1519 Magellan and his fleet set sail from Seville, Spain, to find a water route to the Spice Islands in Indonesia, where the most sought-after commodities -- cloves, pepper, and nutmeg --^\n\nflourished. Most important, they were looking for a passageway, a strait, through the great landmass of the Americas that would lead them to these fabled islands. Laurence Bergreen takes readers on board with Magellan and his crew as they explore, navigate, mutiny, suffer, and die across the seas. He also recounts the many unusual sexual practices the crew experienced, from orgies in Brazil to bizarre customs in the South Pacific. With a fleet of five ships and more than two hundred men, they had set out in search of the Spice Islands. Three years later they returned with an abundance of spices from their intended destination, but with just one ship carrying eighteen emaciated men. They suffered starvation, disease, and torture, and many died, including Magellan, who was violently killed in a fierce battle. A man of great tenacity, cunning, and courage, Magellan was full of contradictions.^\n\nHe was both heroic and foolish, insightful yet blind, a visionary whose instincts outran his ideals. Ambitious to a fault and not above using torture and murder to maintain control of his ships and sailors, he survived innumerable natural hazards in addition to several violent mutinies aboard his own fleet -- and it took no less than the massed forces of fifteen hundred men to kill him. This is the first time in nearly half a century that anyone has attempted to narrate the complete story of Magellan's unprecedented circumnavigation of the globe -- to tell this truly gripping and profoundly important story of heroism, discovery, and disaster. A voyage into history, a tour of the world emerging from the Middle Ages into the Renaissance, an anthropological account of tribes, languages, and customs unknown to Europeans, and a chronicle of a desperate grab for commercial and political power, Over the Edge of the World is a captivating tale that rivals the most exciting thriller fiction."},"latest_revision":17,"revision":17,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2009-05-29T20:14:52.467990"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-08-29T11:01:32.535066"}},{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["3358751"]},"title":"Over the Edge of the World","subtitle":"Magellan's Terrifying Circumnavigation of the Globe","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL387244A"}],"publish_date":"October 14, 2003","publishers":["HarperAudio"],"weight":"5.8 ounces","covers":[30536],"physical_format":"Audio Cassette","subjects":["Explorers","Maritime History","Biography","Audio - Autobiography / Biography","Special Interest - Adventure","History","Abridged Audio - Autobiography/Biography","Audio Adult: Books On Tape","Historical - General","Civilization","Adventurers & Explorers","History / World","Portugal","Voyages around the world","World - General","Audiobooks"],"edition_name":"Abridged edition","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_13":["9780060577261"],"isbn_10":["0060577266"],"oclc_numbers":["53307838"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"7.1 x 4.3 x 1.2 inches","source_records":["amazon:0060577266"],"key":"/books/OL9233817M","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2655768W"}],"latest_revision":8,"revision":8,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-05-07T20:12:05.906833"}},{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["6341513"]},"titl